<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's monetary base down 2.41 pct by Jan 10.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's monetary base down 2.41 pct by Jan 10.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's monetary base fell 2.41 percent to 2.91 billion sucres in the week to January 10, the Central Bank said Monday.</p>
<p>In December 1996, money base grew 12.4 percent to 3.03 billion sucres. The bank gave no reasons for the increase.</p>
<p>The money base ended 1996 at 3.06 billion sucres, up from 2.41 billion sucres at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
</text>
